1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:05,309
This morning, the sea touched the rocks.

2
00:00:05,359 --> 00:00:05,996
But tonight,

3
00:00:06,046 --> 00:00:09,490
it has gone so far away that the boat is sitting on the sand!

4
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:10,800
Where does the sea go?

5
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:13,693
And the next morning, it's back!

6
00:00:13,743 --> 00:00:14,236
In fact,

7
00:00:14,286 --> 00:00:16,680
the sea rises and falls twice a day…

8
00:00:16,730 --> 00:00:18,224
but who is pulling it?

9
00:00:18,992 --> 00:00:20,506
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:23,597
Mini mode!

11
00:00:23,647 --> 00:00:25,972
The Moon pulls on everything on Earth,

12
00:00:26,022 --> 00:00:26,847
just a little.

13
00:00:26,897 --> 00:00:29,222
Rocks don't move, but water can slide:

14
00:00:29,272 --> 00:00:31,585
on the Moon's side, it makes a bulge.

15
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:34,297
And on the other side of the Earth?

16
00:00:34,347 --> 00:00:36,123
There, the Moon pulls less hard,

17
00:00:36,173 --> 00:00:37,949
so the water stays a bit behind…

18
00:00:37,999 --> 00:00:39,710
and that makes a second bulge!

19
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:44,261
And the Earth turns beneath the two bulges.

20
00:00:44,311 --> 00:00:46,809
When your beach passes under a bulge,

21
00:00:46,859 --> 00:00:47,842
it's high tide!

22
00:00:47,892 --> 00:00:49,976
Between the two, it's low tide…

23
00:00:50,026 --> 00:00:50,853
twice a day.

24
00:00:51,638 --> 00:00:53,174
Look, the sea is coming back,

25
00:00:53,224 --> 00:00:54,213
pulled by the Moon!

26
00:00:54,263 --> 00:00:56,509
And even in daytime, when we can't see it,

27
00:00:56,559 --> 00:00:58,692
the Moon is still pulling on the water.

28
00:00:59,470 --> 00:01:01,649
And that's why the sea rises and falls.

29
00:01:03,029 --> 00:01:04,769
The Moon pulls on the ocean's water:

30
00:01:04,819 --> 00:01:07,504
two bulges of water, and the Earth turns beneath them.

31
00:01:08,974 --> 00:01:10,712
With an adult, at the beach:

32
00:01:10,762 --> 00:01:13,011
plant a stick where the sea reaches.

33
00:01:13,061 --> 00:01:15,118
An hour later, the sea has moved…

34
00:01:15,168 --> 00:01:16,955
so, is it rising or falling?

35
00:01:17,732 --> 00:01:20,094
And why does the ground sometimes shake?

36
00:01:20,144 --> 00:01:21,350
The answer tomorrow.
